    <summary>A PDF unlocker for your own files on Windows. It helps you unlock PDF documents, removing print, copy and edit restrictions at once and searching for a forgotten open password locally, so files stay on your computer.</summary>
    <description># PDF password remover for managed Windows PCs

PDF Unlocker - PDF Password Remover Software installs a desktop PDF unlocker to unlock PDF files you own and restore access to them. It clears owner security restrictions on printing, copying and editing, and it searches for a forgotten open password. All processing happens on the local machine, which matters when you deploy a tool across several PCs and need to know it sends nothing out.

![PDF Password Recovery screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ppr/ppr-v1-list.png)

## How to use PDF Unlocker

1. Install the package and open the program.
2. Drag .pdf files into the window, or select PDF files with Add Files and queue a whole directory with Add Folder.
3. Press Start. The quick qpdf path runs first for restrictions and known passwords.
4. A file locked with an open password goes on to a wordlist and then character masks, with progress shown in the background.
5. Check the status per file, choose a destination folder, then save each unlocked file.

Trial note: during the free trial each file is fully processed and displayed in a popup preview, yet saving stays locked until registration. Buying a license lifts that restriction.

![PDF Password Recovery screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ppr/ppr-v1-single.png)

## What the package installs

The package installs the program together with its two engines. The qpdf engine rewrites a PDF without encryption, which is how it can remove restrictions on print, copy and edit instantly, with no password asked. The hashcat engine runs the open-password search, on the graphics card when one is present and on the processor when it is not. A wordlist is included, and the interface comes in English and Russian.

## Who it is for

Anyone who maintains a few PCs or a fleet and gets requests to reopen their own archived PDF documents, such as old contracts, reports or scanned forms. It is meant for documents you are authorized to open. Short and common passwords on older RC4 or AES-128 files come back quickly. To remove PDF password protection on such files is routine work. A long random password on a PDF 2.0 file with AES-256 is not realistic to recover.

![PDF Password Recovery screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ppr/ppr-v1-overwrite.png)

## Trial and license

This package installs the free trial of a commercial program, and full use requires a license. In the trial every file is processed and previewed. The license adds saving the unlocked PDF to a folder. Details on the license options for [PDF Unlocker](https://www.softorbits.net/pdf-password-recovery/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package) are on the product page.

## Frequently asked questions: unlock PDF files

### Which PDF unlocker tool should I choose?

Pick PDF software that runs locally, handles both owner restrictions and open passwords, and is honest about limits. This one works offline, takes batches and says plainly that AES-256 with a long random password cannot be recovered.

### How do I remove PDF password protection?

Add the file and press Start. If the lock is on printing, copying or editing, the qpdf engine clears the permission flags within seconds, and no password is asked for.

### What if I forgot the password to open a PDF?

On a password-protected PDF the search runs a wordlist first, then character masks, with progress listed per file. Human-chosen passwords usually surface sooner than random strings.

### Is it possible to unlock a PDF without knowing its password?

For an owner password, yes, since the program can remove the password from a PDF of that kind directly. An open password has to be recovered by the search, and a GPU speeds that up.
